From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MLD: consider a link missing if its BSS entry is on another
 frequency

wpa_bss_get_usable_links() accepts a neighbor BSS entry that is younger
than WPA_BSS_ML_LINK_FRESH_AGE without a look at its frequency, while
the association takes the link frequency from the RNR of the association
link (wpas_sme_set_mlo_links()). After an AP MLD moved a link to another
channel, the entry of the old channel stays fresh for up to 25 seconds.
cfg80211 knows no BSS on the new channel, so nl80211_assoc_bss() fails
the link with -ENOENT. sme_associate() then lists the link on the BSSID
ignore list and the next attempt goes without it.

Treat such an entry as missing, as an entry that is too old.
wpa_supplicant_connect_ml_missing() then scans the RNR frequency before
the association, and the entry follows the link to the new channel.

The scan runs once for each connection request, since
ml_link_probe_scan() associates without another check. If the entry
stays on the other frequency, for instance with an AP whose RNR
persistently differs from its own channel, wpas_sme_set_mlo_links()
leaves the link out of the association, with no driver failure and no
ignore list entry.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/bss.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/bss.c
@@ -1879,6 +1879,20 @@ u16 wpa_bss_get_usable_links(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s, struct wpa_bss *bss,
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		/* Association uses the RNR frequency, and the driver needs a
+		 * BSS entry on that frequency. */
+		if (bss->mld_links[link_id].freq > 0 &&
+		    neigh_bss->freq != bss->mld_links[link_id].freq) {
+			wpa_dbg(wpa_s, MSG_DEBUG,
+				"MLD: Scan entry for neighbor " MACSTR
+				" is on %d MHz and the RNR reports %d MHz; consider link %u missing",
+				MAC2STR(neigh_bss->bssid), neigh_bss->freq,
+				bss->mld_links[link_id].freq, link_id);
+			if (missing_links)
+				*missing_links |= BIT(link_id);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		/* Check that the affiliated links are for the same AP MLD and
 		 * the information matches */
 		if (!neigh_bss->valid_links) {
